# WHAT IS DRAWN IS WHAT HITS (#76): a swing's stroke is drawn over the ground
# its hit box covers and nowhere else (FightRules.box_hits, MobFx.swing_mesh).
# A harvester at its work on the most open ground there is (`place open_coast`:
# clear of every village and depot, the fewest things near), and the player
# beside its flank facing the way it faces, so the stroke runs past its cutter
# bar over open ground and not over its deck, close in at zoom 9. With
# --hit-areas the frame also outlines what the fight tests: the blow box while
# it is live (magenta) and each body's hit circle (cyan). The stroke is shot
# at the end of its live slice, drawn furthest across its box (`until
# swing_closing`), whatever the tool's timing. Run once per tool, on a fixed
# step so a frame costs the world no time:
#   TOUR_FIXED_FPS=60 tools/tour.sh tours/swing_drawn.tour --seed=4 --hour=12 --weather=clear:0 --give=stave:1 --held=stave --hit-areas
coast calm
wait 0.5
place open_coast
wait 1.2
spawn harvester@180
wait 0.6
zoom 9
near mob:harvester 1.9 along 0.6
wait 0.4
shot 00-beside-its-flank with mob:harvester
tap swing
until swing_closing 1
shot 01-at-the-end-of-its-live-slice with mob:harvester
end
